    "sha": "b3df8f830c40f29a7c26351f91ec94dfd26c2f17",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOPwHItNoAKGIzZGY4ZjgzMGM0MGYyOWE3YzI2MzUxZjkxZWM5NGRmZDI2YzJmMTc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Florian Schmaus",
        "email": "florian.schmaus@codasip.com",
        "date": "2026-02-09T16:21:51Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Florian Schmaus",
        "email": "florian.schmaus@codasip.com",
        "date": "2026-02-11T10:39:40Z"
      },
      "message": "ypermc: clarify that the fixed point is not just a set of permissions\n\nThe existing wording gives the impression that the fixed point only\ndeals with capability permissions. However, if Zyhybrid is available\nand ypermc is used to clear the X permission on a capablity with M=1,\nthen ypermc also legalizes the result by setting M=0.\n\nClarify the wording that ypermc may not only adjust the resulting\npermissions, but also capability metadata, like the M-bit of Zyhybrid.\n\nFixes #941.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florian Schmaus <florian.schmaus@codasip.com>",
